# 1. Agile vs Waterfall – Comparison for Software Testing

| Factor                 | Agile Model                                                            | Waterfall Model                                                         |
| ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Requirements**       | Requirements can change during development based on feedback.          | Requirements are generally finalized at the beginning.                  |
| **Feedback Cycle**     | Feedback is received frequently after every sprint.                    | Feedback usually comes after a major phase or near the end.             |
| **Tester Involvement** | Testers are involved throughout the sprint along with developers.      | Testers usually become more involved after development is completed.    |
| **Documentation**      | Documentation is maintained but the focus is more on working software. | Detailed documentation is prepared at each stage.                       |
| **Flexibility**        | Highly flexible; changes can be included in future sprints.            | Less flexible because changes after a phase is completed can be costly. |

**In short:** Agile supports **continuous testing and feedback**, while Waterfall generally follows a **planned sequence of development and testing phases**.

